/*   Notes:
|
|  Sometimes one runs into a problem where multiple tasks go after the same
|  register on a module in an uncontrolled fashion.  Often, one reads the
|  register, modifies a bit and writes the register.  This should be done
|  in an atomic manner since if another task gets in the middle of these
|  operations, the wrong value will be put into the register.  Since the
|  Motorola CAS(2) instruction isn't portable, we don't want to use it.
|  One way around it is to set things up so that the register is modified
|  in the interrupt service routine by queueing a message and generating a
|  software interrupt for the module in question.  That way only higher IPL
|  ISRs could interfere, but that can be avoided by not allowing them to
|  touch the board in the first place.
|
|  The interrupt level is modifiable without recompiling the code by
|  loading the variable P2RfIntLevel with a value after this driver
|  has been loaded and before P2RF_Init is called.
|
*/



